[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Over the South Pole]
[00:00.92]How was the plane able to clear the mountains? | 飞机是如何能够越过山脉的？
[00:09.25]In 1929, three years after his flight over the North Pole, | 1929年，在他飞越北极三年后，
[00:22.43]the American explorer, R.E. Byrd, | 美国探险家R.E.伯德，
[00:26.80]successfully flew over the South Pole for the first time. | 首次成功飞越了南极。
[00:31.74]Though, at first, Byrd and his men were able to take a | 虽然起初，伯德和他的队员们能够拍摄到
[00:36.98]great many photographs of the mountains that lay below, | 许多下方山脉的照片，
[00:41.72]they soon ran into serious trouble. | 但他们很快就遇到了严重的麻烦。
[00:45.56]At one point, it seemed certain that their plane would crash. | 有一刻，他们的飞机似乎肯定会坠毁。
[00:51.08]It could only get over the mountains if it rose to 10, 000 feet. | 只有当飞机上升到10,000英尺时，才能越过山脉。
[00:57.20]Byrd at once ordered his men to throw out two heavy food sacks. | 伯德立即命令他的队员们扔掉两个沉重的食物袋。
[01:03.68]The plane was then able to rise and it cleared the mountains by 400 feet. | 飞机随后得以升高，并以400英尺的高度越过了山脉。
[01:10.46]Byrd now knew that he would be able to reach the South Pole which was 300 miles away, | 伯德现在知道他将能够抵达300英里外的南极，
[01:18.36]for there were no more mountains in sight. | 因为视线中没有更多的山脉了。
[01:22.03]The aircraft was able to fly over the endless white plains without difficulty. | 飞机能够毫不费力地飞越无尽的白色平原。